<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
           elementFormDefault="qualified">

  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
RESPONSE schema for updateCustomerB (Customer360) -- rebuilt 2026-10-12 against the
loyalty-app service generation.

Namespace: the service writes the RESPONSE document without any XML namespace, so this schema
has no target namespace. Earlier revisions declared one, which no real response could satisfy.

The response is a FLAT list of elements under RESPONSE. The service builds it incrementally,
so the ORDER of the children varies by code path and RESPONSE_DATE / RESPONSE_CODE /
RESPONSE_DATA can occur more than once (see "double outcome" below). The content is therefore
modelled as a free, repeatable choice.

Typical shapes
  Updated  : [LOYALTY_ID] RESPONSE_DATE CUSTOMER_ID RESPONSE_CODE=S102
  Created  : RESPONSE_DATE CUSTOMER_ID [LOYALTY_ID] RESPONSE_CODE=S103
  Rejected : RESPONSE_DATE [CUSTOMER_ID] [echo of the offending value] RESPONSE_CODE=Exxx
  Failed   : RESPONSE_DATE [CUSTOMER_ID] RESPONSE_CODE=Exxx RESPONSE_DATA   (RESPONSE_DATA may precede the code)
  No tenant: RESPONSE_CODE=E888 only (no RESPONSE_DATE)
  Fallback : RESPONSE_DATE (empty) RESPONSE_CODE=E999, no ResponseId
ALWAYS read the outcome from RESPONSE_CODE; when it occurs more than once the LAST one is the
final outcome. Every handled outcome is HTTP 200.

Double outcome: an update can report S102 and then fail while saving. The document then
carries a second RESPONSE_DATE, a second RESPONSE_CODE (E1006) and RESPONSE_DATA after the S102.

CUSTOMER_ID in an error response is the customer the request was resolved to at that point
(sent, or found by the duplicate check); it is omitted when none had been resolved.

RESPONSE_CODE catalog (xs:string ON PURPOSE -- an open set, new codes must not break validation)
 Success
  S102 existing customer updated          S103 new customer created
 Input
  E101 XmlInput empty                     E102 malformed XML (detail in RESPONSE_DATA)
  E103 parser configuration (RESPONSE_DATA)   E104 I/O error reading the input (RESPONSE_DATA)
  E201 BIRTHDAY not in an accepted format
  E222 EMAIL fails the e-mail format check
  E223 a required value was sent EMPTY: FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, postal ZIPCODE (echoed as ZIPCODE)
       or EMAIL (echoed as EMAIL)
  E106 STATE unknown (echoed as STATE), or STATE does not belong to COUNTRY (echoed as COUNTRY)
  E107 COUNTRY unknown (echoed as COUNTRY)
  E166 Canadian postal code invalid (echoed as ZIP_CODE)
  E127 STORE_ID / ASSIGNED_STORE / PREFERRED_STORE / LOYALTY_STORE not a known store
 Identity and loyalty
  E162 a cross-reference identifier in the request already belongs to another customer
  E163 the primary phone number is on the blocked-number list
  E224 the primary phone number is already the primary phone of another customer
  E128 LOYALTY_ID (or WINDSS_ID) already assigned to another customer
  E129 ATG_CUST_ID already assigned to another customer
  E131 customer already has a different ATG_CUST_ID      E132 customer already has a different WINDSS_ID
  E133 LOYALTY_ID not numeric, or all zeros
 Processing
  E108 customer creation failed unexpectedly (RESPONSE_DATA)
  E110 no customer resolved for the update      E111 customer record not found for the update
  E112 create/identifier storage failed (RESPONSE_DATA)
  E1006 a processing step failed (RESPONSE_DATA carries the detail)
 Gate
  E888 X-tenant-Key header missing or empty (the operation did not run)
  E899 accessTokenKey validation failed (the operation did not run)
  E999 unhandled failure (fixed fallback document)
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Wrapper seen on gate-level failures of sibling operations (WEBSERVICE/RESPONSE,
without ResponseId). Not produced by this operation's handler on the loyalty-app service generation, which answers
E888 and E899 with a bare RESPONSE root; declared so that such a document still validates.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element ref="RESPONSE"/>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Top-level response container; flat, order-free (see the schema header).</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:element ref="RESPONSE_DATE"/>
        <xs:element ref="RESPONSE_CODE"/>
        <xs:element ref="RESPONSE_DATA"/>
        <xs:element ref="CUSTOMER_ID"/>
        <xs:element ref="LOYALTY_ID"/>
        <xs:element ref="STATE"/>
        <xs:element ref="COUNTRY"/>
        <xs:element ref="ZIPCODE"/>
        <xs:element ref="ZIP_CODE"/>
        <xs:element ref="EMAIL"/>
      </xs:choice>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server-side request-log correlation id. Present on every response built by the
service (including E888 and E899); absent on the E999 fallback document.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server timestamp, format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" with 1 to 3 fractional digits
(e.g. 2026-10-12 15:01:02.655). Deliberately xs:string: not ISO 8601. Absent on E888; empty on the E999 fallback.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Outcome code. Unlike the read operations, updateCustomerB sends a code on success too
(S102 / S103). See the catalog in the schema header. If repeated, the last occurrence is the final outcome.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATA" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Free-text failure detail (an internal error message), sent with E102, E103, E104, E108,
E112 and E1006. May be EMPTY when the underlying failure carried no message. For diagnostics only; do not parse.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>On S102: the customer that was updated. On S103: the identifier of the NEWLY CREATED
customer -- store it. On errors: the customer the request had been resolved to, when any.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="LOYALTY_ID" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Loyalty identifier now attached to the customer. Sent only when the loyalty program is
switched on for the environment and this request assigned, replaced or generated a loyalty identifier. On an update
it is written BEFORE RESPONSE_DATE.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="STATE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Echo of the rejected STATE value (E106, unknown state/province).</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="COUNTRY" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Echo of the COUNTRY value: with E107 the country is unknown; with E106 the STATE sent
does not belong to this country.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="ZIPCODE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Echo sent with E223 when the postal ZIPCODE was sent empty (or was missing from a postal
contact that needed a new address record) -- so this element is itself EMPTY.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="ZIP_CODE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Echo of the rejected postal code (E166, invalid Canadian postal code), upper-cased.
Note the different spelling from ZIPCODE: both are sent by the service, on different errors.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="EMAIL" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Echo sent with E223 when an e-mail contact was sent with an empty or missing EMAIL
-- so this element is itself EMPTY.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
